#[navbar]

#[section, $md:
    @../ (Documentation) / MON format

    # MON format

    MON means Moth Object Notation. **MON syntax** names Moth's shared
    parenthesised argument and value-construction notation.
    **The MON format** is the separate serialised-data profile with its own
    supported values and serialisation rules.

    Serialised MON is literal data only. A MON reader never evaluates Moth
    expressions, including foldable ones. Availability is Rust-only: the
    Rust-facing codec contract is accepted and queued, and Moth-native
    operations remain deferred separately.
]

